# Deployment & Environment

## Env files (root)

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `.env.example` | Local dev template |
| `.env.staging.example` | Staging template |
| `.env` / `.env.staging` | **Not committed** — secrets |

Required vars: `DB_CONNECTION_STRING`, `ENCRYPTION_KEY`, `JWT_SECRET`, `RABBITMQ_PASS`, `EMAIL_*`, `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS`

## Docker Compose

| File | Use |
|------|-----|
| `docker-compose.yml` | Local full stack |
| `docker-compose.staging.yml` | VPS staging |
| `docker-compose.override.yml` | Local overrides |

Services: `qalam-api` (8080), `messaging-api`, `rabbitmq`, `qalam-admin`, `qalam-teacher`

## Local dev (PowerShell, from root)

```powershell
.\scripts\dev\run-rabbitmq.ps1
.\scripts\dev\run-messaging-api.ps1   # :62901
.\scripts\dev\run-api.ps1             # :62900
.\scripts\dev\run-admin.ps1           # :3005
.\scripts\dev\run-teacher.ps1         # :3000
```

Scripts load root `.env`.

## Migrations

- Staging: `MIGRATE_ON_STARTUP=true` allowed
- Production: manual migration gate — see `docs/OPERATIONS_RUNBOOK.md`

## CI

GitHub Actions must use `submodules: recursive` to build frontends.

## Do not

- Commit `.env`, `.env.staging`, or production credentials
- Force-push to main/master without explicit approval
- Run prod migrations without following `docs/OPERATIONS_RUNBOOK.md`
